-- title:
--   Adic base data at a place of ℚ̄ above q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $N$ a natural number not divisible by $q$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Write $C_A$ for the completion of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at the valuation of $A$ and $K_0 =$ `ratClosure A` for the topological closure of the prime subfield of $C_A$. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformiser of $K_0$ relative to $C_A$, that is, an element $\varpi.\varpi \in K_0$ whose valuation in $C_A$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and such that every nonzero $a \in K_0$ satisfies $v(\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi)^{-N}$ for some $N \in \mathbb N$; assume the image of $\varpi.\varpi$ in $C_A$ is the image of $q$. Then there exist: a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O_0$ with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O_0/\pi) = q$ and $(q) = (\pi)$, equipped with an algebra structure over which $K_0$ is its fraction field; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O_0$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, together with an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ such that $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^q \pmod \pi$ for all $x$, such that every $x \in \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O_0$ modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$; a homomorphism $v\!\det \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with $v\!\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^n$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O_0$; and a ring homomorphism $\psi_0 \colon \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to C_A$, satisfying: $\pi$ maps to $\varpi.\varpi$ in $K_0$; $N$ is a unit of $\mathcal O_0$; the image of $\mathcal O_0$ in $K_0$ is exactly $\{x : v(x) \le 1 \text{ in } C_A\}$; $v(\psi_0(y)) \le 1$ for all $y$; $\psi_0$ restricted along $\mathcal O_0 \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ agrees with $\mathcal O_0 \to K_0 \to C_A$; and, for all $x, y \in C_A$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \ne 0$, there is $n \in \mathbb N$ with $v(x)^n \le v(y)$.
--
--   This packages, in a single existential statement, the local base data attached to a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $q$: the ring of integers $\mathbb Z_q$ inside the $q$-adic closure of $\mathbb Q$ in $C_A$, an unramified completion with its Frobenius, the determinant valuation on $\mathrm{GL}_2$, and the compatible embedding into $C_A$. It is used by the Čerednik–Drinfel'd descent and intertwining constructions, which obtain all of this data at once.
